From 9bfc484ff13bd318e40acead64b9df2cec97b9fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 11:30:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: q6_K MMVQ route DEFAULT ON for n=7,8 on AMD; strike
 the n=2,3 clause the duplicate-case parser manufactured

STRIKE. The n=2/n=3 at k>8192 clause R71 shipped is removed. test-backend-ops emits every n=1..8 case TWICE per run and r71-parse.py silently kept the LAST occurrence, so 5120x17408 n=3 published as 1.0463 (5/6, ADMIT) when its first occurrence is 0.9945 (2/6, a LOSS) -- the admit rested on which of two identical cases got overwritten (CHECK-R71 finding 1). n=2 admits on all three picks but rests on ONE shape with a 0.98 worst round, and the served file's other k>8192 shape (5120x10240) was never measured. Neither is shippable. The admission is now exactly the cells that admit on first, mean AND last at every measured shape: !is_id && (n == 7 || n == 8).

FLIP. Default becomes device-probed: route on AMD, legacy on every other vendor (UNMEASURED there, and the registry row says so). Same device test the q5_K route uses, because the admit is itself fenced to VK_VENDOR_ID_AMD. Basis: n=7,8 won 36/36 paired rounds across every timed shape and every occurrence pick, worst single round 1.003, and both PPL gates sit inside one stderr. R71 held the default OFF because the qualifying widths are a non-contiguous island the row geometry does not explain -- that reading is NOT withdrawn and is still the brief for a q6_K shader lane (f32 cliff at n=6,7; MMVQ cliff at n=5,6; n=7,8 is the gap between them) -- but an inelegant explanation is not a reason to leave a measured, quality-gated win switched off. GGML_ARIFI_Q6K_MMVQ=legacy restores the pre-R71b route on one binary.

TEST CASES. 5120x6144 (x10 tensors, 1.49 percent of the served file, and the only k between 5120 and 17408 anything is measured at) and 1024x5120 (x15 tensors, small m, the row-geometry end) had NO case at all, so R71 recorded 0 cells for the first and never asked for the second. Both added -- and to BOTH lists: the lane-236 q6_K rows went into make_test_cases_eval() only, so perf never had them either.

BANNER. The =1 diagnostic used to print "legacy (default)" while forcing q6_K to MMVQ at every width, the opposite of what the binary does (CHECK-R71 finding 10). It now names itself.

Origin: lane-256 R71b, CHECK-R71 PASS-GATED ruling
Measured-effect: n=7,8 win 36/36 paired rounds on the three R71 shapes and all three occurrence picks (medians 1.400/1.122/1.163 at n=7, 1.131/1.085/1.050 at n=8, worst single round 1.003), plus G2 on the two previously untestable served shapes 5120x6144 (1.1254 6/6, 1.0576 5/6) and 1024x5120 (1.0876 6/6, 1.0087 5/6) with no measured loss anywhere; PPL inside one stderr at -b 8 (5.9932 vs 5.9945) and -b 7 (5.9897 vs 5.9947)
Lane: lane-256
Cherry-picked-from: e9f69f128 (ArifiLabs lane-256 R71, onto arifi/main 94461e770)
