@@ -68,7 +68,7 @@ safe measurement posture.
 | `GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_A_HOIST_IQ1` | **OFF when unset.** Only an exact `1` turns the A-side hoist on for the `IQ1_S` and `IQ1_M` `q8_1` pipelines, and never above the global switch — `GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_A_HOIST=0` forces it off regardless. Added 2026-09-14 (lane-235/R48b). | Scope: the `IQ1_S` and `IQ1_M` `q8_1` `mul_mat_vec` pipelines only. They carry the largest A state of any MMVQ type (10 and 12 registers per row against 5-6 for the K-quants) and run the most rows per workgroup (`rm_iq_int` = 4 or 8), the highest product in the register table. Gated in the HOST, not by an `#ifdef`: the shader keeps both paths, so no rebuild moves it. | Only to pair the IQ1 types specifically. | **UNMEASURED on these two types — that is exactly why they ship OFF.** The default is a register-pressure judgement (report section 3 of `OPUS-R48B-MMVQ-A-HOIST-REPORT.md`), not a measurement. Arithmetic is identical either way; correctness is covered by the same `MUL_MAT` sweep. |
 | `GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_ROUTE` | **unset = R48b routing.** Only the exact string `legacy` pins `ggml_vk_should_use_mmvq()` back to the pre-R48b rules while KEEPING the hoisted nest. Added 2026-09-14 (lane-235/R48b phase 2). | Scope: two AMD routing rules, and nothing else. (i) `GGML_TYPE_SX8` → MMVQ at every width (`legacy`: opt-in via `GGML_ARIFI_SX8_MMVQ=1`). (ii) `GGML_TYPE_Q4_K` at `n >= 5` → MMVQ when `k <= 8192`, f32 above (`legacy`: f32 at every `n >= 5`). `Q5_K`, `Q8_0` and the legacy-block family are untouched in both modes. Both rules are additionally gated on the hoist being live, so on a non-AMD device or under `GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_A_HOIST=0` they are already the legacy rules. **`legacy` is NOT the same arm as `GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_A_HOIST=0`**: this one keeps the hoisted nest and changes only where traffic is sent, the other removes the nest as well. A pairing log must say which was used. | Use `legacy` to pair the ROUTING change alone, holding the kernel constant. | **Routing derived from the HQ forced-MMVQ pairing, not yet re-measured at default routing.** `q4_K` MMVQ+hoist vs the f32 default at `n=5..8`: 248320x5120 (k=5120) `55.7/52.1/48.0/45.6` vs `46.0/36.1/35.0/29.0` GB/s (**+21/+44/+37/+57%**), 17408x5120 (k=5120) `35.7/34.8/33.5/31.3` vs `33.2/27.9/29.9/24.4` (win), 5120x17408 (**k=17408**) `32.4/26.8/24.3/22.7` vs `37.0/30.8/31.6/27.2` (**LOSS**) — hence the `k` split. `k = 8192` is the midpoint of the two measured `k` values and is an **untested boundary**: nothing was run between 5120 and 17408. S-X8 evidence is in the `GGML_ARIFI_SX8_MMVQ` row above. |
 | `GGML_ARIFI_Q5K_MMVQ` | **DEFAULT `route` on AMD, `legacy` on every other vendor — flipped 2026-09-18 (lane-254/R66 step 2a, President ruling: a proven-safe gain ships ON).** The device probe is the one `ggml_vk_should_use_mmvq()` already applies (the whole Q5_K arm sits inside `vendor_id == VK_VENDOR_ID_AMD && n > 1`), so Intel-class and NVIDIA devices — where this was never measured — keep `legacy` and say so on the startup line. `GGML_ARIFI_Q5K_MMVQ=legacy` restores the pre-R66 route on one binary; the exact string `route` admits `GGML_TYPE_Q5_K` to the A-hoisted `q8_1` MMVQ mat-vec at **`n=5..8` and `k <= 8192`**; every other `n` and every larger `k` still take the f32 dequant shader, exactly as today. The string `v2` is accepted as a NAME only and behaves as `legacy`: it is reserved for a shader change this lane did not need, and the device-init line says so out loud rather than letting a caller think it routed. Added 2026-09-17 (lane-252/R64). | Scope: the `Q5_K` arm of `ggml_vk_should_use_mmvq()` on AMD at `n > 1`, and nothing else. Additionally gated on `mmvq_a_hoist` being live and on `GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_ROUTE != legacy`, so on a non-AMD device or with the hoist off it is already the legacy rule. **NOT bit-identical to `legacy` by construction** — the MMVQ path quantises B to `q8_1` and does an integer dot, where the f32 route does float madds; this is a different arithmetic, not a scheduling change, and no pairing may describe it as one. Device-init receipt on stderr: `ggml_vulkan: q5_k mmvq route: route (n=5..8, k<=8192)` / `legacy`. | **Leave it at the default until HQ has paired it served.** Set `route` to A/B the arms on one binary. The `n>=5` and `k<=8192` boundaries are **gfx1103 measurements, not portable constants** — both are re-derivable and both must be re-paired on another device class. | **MEASURED op-level, 6 interleaved rounds, one quiet hold, paired per round; served t/s UNMEASURED by the maker.** 17408x5120 (`r64-evidence/13-paired-ffn.txt`, `13-paired-ffn2.txt`), `default/route` median [min..max] wins/6: `n=5` **1.067** [1.032..1.104] 6/6, `n=6` **1.109** 6/6, `n=7` **1.095** 6/6, `n=8` **1.204** [1.185..1.266] 6/6; `n=1` 0.999 (untouched). `marg(4..8)` falls **113.8 → 5.4 us/col** against q4_K's 27 — the lane's ship criterion. Re-taken on the shipped `n>=5` binary: `n=5..8` = 1.056/1.120/1.075/1.152, 5-6/6. **The `k` gate is measured, not copied**: at 5120x17408 (`k=17408`) forced MMVQ **LOSES**, unanimously at `n=5` (0.962 [0.921..0.997], **0/6** rounds won) and near-unanimously at `n=6` (0.968, 1/6); at `n=7`/`n=8` the medians are 0.988/0.976 but the rounds split 3/6 and 2/6 and the ranges straddle 1.0, so those two are **not** established against the null band and are not claimed (`13-paired-down-head.txt`). The gate ships on the firm end, and its error direction is to NARROW the admit. On the served Q4_K_XL file **90.5% of Q5_K bytes sit at `k<=8192`** (`11-typemix.txt`), so the gate keeps nearly all of the type. **The `n<5` end is NOT established as a loss**: the shipped binary makes `route` at `n=1..4` the identical code path to `default`, and it still read 0.942 at `n=4` — a three-arm null control (`14-null-table.txt`, all legacy, same slots) bounds the slot artifact at only 1-3%, so `n=4` on this shape is **noise-dominated and the lane's least-resolved cell**. `n>=5` is the conservative bound, not a fitted one: it is where `rm_int_n()` gives the MMVQ pipeline 4 rows per workgroup instead of 1. Correctness `test -o MUL_MAT -p type_a=q5_K/q6_K` **152 cases (q5_K 85/85 + q6_K 67/67), 0 FAIL, all three arms** (`20-correct-*`), full `MUL_MAT` sweep **2130/2130, 0 FAIL both arms** (`21-mulmat-full-*`), planted RED in `mul_mat_vecq.comp` under `DATA_A_Q5_K && NUM_COLS>1` gives **52/85 = 33 FAIL cases with `route`, every one at `n=5..8`, and 85/85 with `legacy`**, restored byte-identical (`40-restore-proof.txt`). 27B text: **6/6 token-identical**, 3 greedy prompts x 2 Q4_K_XL files — but that is an `n=1` decode, where this rule is **inert by construction**, so it is a no-regression receipt and NOT evidence about the routed arithmetic. **The ship rule is now discharged, by HQ and not by the maker (chain149):** PPL **at batch 8, where the route is actually exercised** (a default-batch cell runs at n=512 through `mul_mm` and would have been inert) reads **5.9918 legacy vs 5.9932 route against +/-0.143** - identical inside one stderr; served Q4_K_XL DFlash2 **tie**, plain arm **noise**, rolled40 **37/37**. Receipts under `2026-09-14-lane-234-r48-kernels/100-r64-q5k-route/` and `2026-09-02-lane-209/r64-lane-252/c24-q4kxl-27b/SEAT/AB.json`. **Expected served effect is small by construction and a large one would be a red flag:** ~**+0.7% at n=5**, ceiling ~**+1.8% at n=8**, **0% at n=4** (inert) - so a tie IS the predicted result, and a gain above ~2% means the attribution is wrong, not the lever better. **Moving the default remains an independent checker's call.** |
-| `GGML_ARIFI_Q6K_MMVQ` | **DEFAULT `legacy` on EVERY vendor, including AMD — the default does NOT move (F-08), and that is the deliberate outcome of lane-256/R71, not an omission.** Four accepted values, and the two numeric ones keep their original R48c meaning exactly: unset or `legacy` = `GGML_TYPE_Q6_K` stays on the f32 dequant mat-vec `mul_mat_vec_q6_k_f32_f32` (`ggml-vulkan.cpp:7555`) at every width; `route` = the measured R71 admit, **MUL_MAT only, `n=7` or `n=8` at any `k`, plus `n=2` or `n=3` at `k > 8192`**; `1` = the R48c *diagnostic* that forces MMVQ at **every** width and ignores the admit (this is the arm R71's own decider table used, and it reaches `MUL_MAT_ID` as well); `0` = the R48c diagnostic that forces it off even on Intel. Added `route`/`legacy` 2026-09-19 (lane-256/R71); the `0`/`1` lever is from 2026-09-13 (lane-236/R48c). | Scope: the `GGML_TYPE_Q6_K` arm of `ggml_vk_should_use_mmvq_impl()`, which sits at `ggml-vulkan.cpp:12344` **above** the `vendor_id == AMD && n > 1` block that holds the Q5_K and Q4_K admits — q6_K exits there and never reaches that block, so this admit could not be written in the same place or the same shape as the Q5_K one. Additionally gated on `vendor_id == VK_VENDOR_ID_AMD` (the only vendor measured) and on `!is_id`. **`MUL_MAT_ID` is fenced out of `route` on evidence, not on caution** — R71 added an `is_id` flag to this predicate because `MUL_MAT` (`:12656`) and `MUL_MAT_ID` (`:13944`) share it, and the `_id` `q8_1` pipeline is a different pipeline with no `NUM_COLS` dimension (`pipeline_dequant_mul_mat_vec_id_q8_1_f32`, `:1606`/`:7743`) so a plain-path width rule says nothing about it. **NOT bit-identical to `legacy` by construction** — MMVQ quantises the activation to `q8_1` and does an integer dot where the f32 route does float madds; that is different arithmetic, not a scheduling change. Device-init receipt on stderr: `ggml_vulkan: q6_k mmvq route: route (MUL_MAT only: n=7,8 any k; n=2,3 at k>8192)` / `legacy`. | **Leave it at `legacy`.** Set `route` to A/B the arms on one binary, `1` to reproduce R71's decider arm. The widths and the `k > 8192` boundary are gfx1103 measurements, not portable constants. | **MEASURED op-level, one binary, 6 interleaved and counterbalanced rounds, paired per round, bar pre-registered at `08907df1b` BEFORE the first round (admit = ≥5/6 rounds won AND median ≥ 1.03; a LOSS is never admitted). Served t/s UNMEASURED by the maker.** `default/mmvq` median [min..max] wins/6, `r71-evidence/13-paired.txt`: **248320x5120** `n=7` **1.400** [1.337..1.409] 6/6, `n=8` **1.131** 6/6 — but `n=4` 0.909 0/6 and `n=5` **0.735** 0/6; **17408x5120** `n=7` **1.122** 6/6, `n=8` **1.085** 6/6, `n=1` 1.043 6/6 — `n=2..5` all lose; **5120x17408** `n=7` **1.163** 6/6, `n=8` **1.050** 6/6, `n=2` 1.054 5/6, `n=3` 1.046 5/6 — `n=5` **0.914** 0/6, `n=6` 0.958 1/6. 24 plain cells executed: 11 admit, 12 loss. **WHY IT SHIPS OFF:** the qualifying widths are a non-contiguous island and the row geometry does not explain them. Geometry alone predicts a clean flip at `n=5` — the f32 shader runs `rm_kq` = 2 rows at every width (`:7555`) against the MMVQ `rm_int_n(rm_kq_int=1, i)` = 1 row at `NUM_COLS <= 4` and 4 at `>= 5` (`:7666`), the same pair that made the Q5_K `n>=5` admit a rule — and `n=5` is instead the **worst** cell on all three shapes. The raw us/run show two shaders with two different width cliffs (f32 jumps at `n=6,7`: 13882 → 20967 → 20046 us on 248320x5120; MMVQ jumps at `n=5,6`: 15245 → 20971 → 21121), so the `n=7,8` win is the gap between two defects, not evidence MMVQ is the right route. That makes both cliffs the brief for a q6_K **shader** lane, and makes flipping this default an independent checker's call — the same standing `GGML_ARIFI_ROCMFP4_MMVQ` is held to. **`MUL_MAT_ID` is a WASH, measured: 26 executed `_id` cells over the same 6 rounds gave 1 admit, 9 losses, and ~1.00 medians on the rest (`r71-evidence/16-paired-id.txt`)** — which matters because **88% of Ornith-1.5-35B-A3B's q6_K bytes, 21.3% of that whole file, are expert tensors on that path** (`r71-evidence/11-q6k-shapes.txt`). **UNMEASURED:** every non-AMD vendor, the served token level, `m=5120 k=6144` (test-backend-ops carries no such `MUL_MAT` case, so that cell executed **0** rows and is reported as absent, not as a tie), and any `k` between 5120 and 17408. |
+| `GGML_ARIFI_Q6K_MMVQ` | **DEFAULT `route` on AMD, `legacy` on every other vendor — flipped 2026-09-19 (lane-256/R71b, on CHECK-R71's PASS-GATED ruling and the President's law that a PPL-gated, never-slower-here gain ships ON).** The device probe is the same one the `GGML_ARIFI_Q5K_MMVQ` row above uses, and for the same reason: the admit itself is fenced to `VK_VENDOR_ID_AMD`, the only vendor any of this was measured on, so Intel-class and NVIDIA keep `legacy` — **that is UNMEASURED, not a judgement about those devices** — and the startup line says which. Four accepted values; the two numeric ones keep their original R48c meaning exactly. `route` = the measured admit, **MUL_MAT only, `n == 7` or `n == 8`, any `m`, any `k`**; `legacy` = `GGML_TYPE_Q6_K` stays on the f32 dequant mat-vec `mul_mat_vec_q6_k_f32_f32` (`:7555`) at every width, which restores the pre-R71b route on one binary; `1` = the R48c *diagnostic* that forces MMVQ at **every** width, bypasses the admit and **does** reach `MUL_MAT_ID`; `0` = the R48c diagnostic that forces it off on every vendor. **The `n=2`/`n=3` at `k > 8192` clause R71 shipped is STRUCK** — see the evidence column. Added `route`/`legacy` 2026-09-19 (lane-256/R71); default flipped and clause struck the same day (lane-256/R71b); the `0`/`1` lever is from 2026-09-13 (lane-236/R48c). | Scope: the `GGML_TYPE_Q6_K` arm of `ggml_vk_should_use_mmvq_impl()`, which sits at `ggml-vulkan.cpp:12344` **above** the `vendor_id == AMD && n > 1` block holding the Q5_K and Q4_K admits — q6_K exits there and never reaches that block, so this admit could not be written in the same place or the same shape as the Q5_K one. Additionally gated on `vendor_id == VK_VENDOR_ID_AMD` and on `!is_id`. **`MUL_MAT_ID` is fenced out of `route` on evidence, not on caution** — R71 added an `is_id` flag because `MUL_MAT` (`:12656`) and `MUL_MAT_ID` (`:13944`) share this predicate, and the `_id` `q8_1` pipeline is a different pipeline with no `NUM_COLS` dimension (`:1606`/`:7743`), so a plain-path width rule says nothing about it. **NOT bit-identical to `legacy` by construction** — MMVQ quantises the activation to `q8_1` and does an integer dot where the f32 route does float madds; different arithmetic, not a scheduling change, and no pairing may describe it as one. Device-init receipt on stderr: `ggml_vulkan: q6_k mmvq route: route (MUL_MAT only, n=7..8) (device-probe)` / `legacy`, and the `=1` diagnostic now names itself on that line instead of mislabelling itself `legacy` (CHECK-R71 finding 10). | **Leave it at the default.** Set `legacy` to A/B the arms on one binary, `1` to reproduce the R48c force-everything arm. The `n=7,8` widths are gfx1103 measurements, not portable constants, and must be re-derived on another device class. | **MEASURED op-level, one binary, 6 interleaved and counterbalanced rounds, paired per round, bar pre-registered at `08907df1b` BEFORE the first round (admit = ≥5/6 rounds won AND median ≥ 1.03; a LOSS is never admitted). Served t/s UNMEASURED.** **`n=7,8` won 36/36 paired rounds across all three R71 shapes AND all three occurrence picks, worst single round 1.003.** `default/mmvq` medians, `r71-evidence/13-paired.txt`: **248320x5120** `n=7` **1.400**, `n=8` **1.131**; **17408x5120** `n=7` **1.122**, `n=8` **1.085**; **5120x17408** `n=7` **1.163**, `n=8` **1.050** — all 6/6. **G2 (R71b) closed the two SERVED shapes that had no test case at all** (`82-paired-g2.txt`, arms = the shipped `legacy`/`route`, not the `=1` diagnostic): **5120x6144** `n=7` **1.1254** 6/6, `n=8` **1.0576** 5/6; **1024x5120** `n=7` **1.0876** 6/6, `n=8` 1.0087 5/6 (a wash at small `m`, but **no measured loss**, so no `m`/`k` fence was added). **The struck clause, and why:** `test-backend-ops` emits every `n=1..8` case **twice** per run and the R71 parser silently kept the **last** occurrence; re-parsed per occurrence, `5120x17408 n=3` is **0.9945 (2/6, a LOSS)** on the first and 1.0463 (5/6) on the last — a published admit that